Subject: [PATCH] drm/sched: guard cleanup timestamp updates in the v7 backport

Panthor supplies unbound submission workqueues, so submission and cleanup
work can overlap. drm_sched_job_begin() publishes a job to pending_list
before run_job() returns and its scheduled fence is signaled. Cleanup of
an older finished job can therefore see an unsignaled next job and write
the old completion timestamp over the next fence's callback-list union.

job_list_lock protects the pending entry and its fence lifetime, but does
not serialize that write with dma_fence_signal(). SIGNALED_BIT alone is
insufficient: the signal path sets it before detaching the callback list.
Require DMA_FENCE_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_BIT, which is set only after the signal
path has replaced the callback list with the timestamp and stays set for
the remaining fence lifetime. A false result safely skips only the timing
refinement; timeout rearming remains unchanged.

Backport the same guard used by drm_sched_get_finished_job() in the pinned
Linux v7.0 donor. Keep the existing job-list lock and fence reference
ownership; add no fence-lock nesting, KMI layout, or submission changes.

Upstream donor: 028ef9c96e96197026887c0f092424679298aae8
Upstream file: drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
Google base: 3c76c2d71bb32039037c6f5dc38b172fe4142bdb
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
@@ -1276,8 +1276,10 @@
 						typeof(*next), list);
 
 		if (next) {
-			next->s_fence->scheduled.timestamp =
-				dma_fence_timestamp(&job->s_fence->finished);
+			if (test_bit(DMA_FENCE_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_BIT,
+				     &next->s_fence->scheduled.flags))
+				next->s_fence->scheduled.timestamp =
+					dma_fence_timestamp(&job->s_fence->finished);
 			/* start TO timer for next job */
 			drm_sched_start_timeout(sched);
 		}
